==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|haldan}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*haldaną||to watch, look after}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|halda}} ({{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|hâlde}}), {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|haldan}} ({{etyl|nds|-}} {{m|nds|holen}}), {{etyl|odt|-}} {{m|odt|haldan}} ({{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|houden}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|haltan}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|halten}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|halda}} ({{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|hålla}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|holde}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌷𐌰𐌻𐌳𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhæɑldɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# to keep watch over (cattle etc.)
# to [[hold]] fast, to [[grasp]]
# to [[contain]]
# to [[possess]]
# {{context|intransitive|lang=ang}} to maintain one’s position against an enemy

